quran[15]{c,v,t}:
  19,96,"As for those who believe and perform righteous deeds, the Most-Compassionate (Lord) will endear them (to His creation)."
  19,97,"Indeed, We have made this (Qur’an) easy in your tongue (i.e. in Arabic) so, with it, you may give glad tidings to the God-conscious and warn the contentious people through it."
  19,98,And how many a generation We destroyed before them! Can you trace any of them or (even) hear the slightest murmuring sound from them?
  20,1,Ta-Ha.
  20,2,(Esteemed Prophet!) We have not revealed the Qur’an to you that you should be distressed.
  20,3,(We revealed it) only as a reminder for the one who fears (his Lord).
  20,4,(It is) a revelation from the One Who created the earth and the highest heavens.
  20,5,The Most-Compassionate (Lord) established (His authority) over the Throne (befitting His Glory).
  20,6,"To Him belongs whatever is in the heavens and whatever is on the earth, whatever is in between them and whatever is under the ground."
  20,7,"Whether you speak loudly (or quietly), He certainly knows what is secret and what is even more hidden."
  20,8,Allah—there is no god except Him. To Him belong the most Beautiful Names.
  20,9,And has the story of Musa (Moses) come to you (O Prophet)?
  20,10,"When he saw a fire (on his way back to Egypt from Madyan), he said to his family: ‘Stay here! Indeed, I have seen a fire. Perhaps I may bring you a flaming brand from it or find some guidance at the fire.’"
  20,11,"So, when he approached it, he was called: ‘O Musa (Moses)!"
  20,12,"Indeed, I am your Lord! So take off your sandals. Indeed, you are in the sacred valley of Tuwa."
